+// S2Arm 2026-11-18 probe3: pure observation.  Nothing here changes what is drawn; every probe
+// only reads what the renderer already produced and every buffer / texture readback is small
+// (<= 8x8 texels and <= 256 bytes, or <= 128 bytes per buffer blit).
+//   [dump]    swapschain: pre (before the composite pass, key 5da03adb), mid (after it), post
+//             (after the UI pass, key ec8ccd7a) -> <dir>/rop972_<stage>_<ser>.png
+//   [lightbuf] light_cull compute output buffer (key f9def5d9): first 64 / middle 64 / offset-0 u32
+//   [hiz]    the 800x450 R8 / depth input the light_cull dispatch binds (mip chain)
+//   [litout] the 1600x900 R11G11B10F / RG32 render pass that samples the G-buffer
+//   [gdraw]  one line per G-buffer writer draw, its fragment texture slots and cb0[0..3]
+//   [gbtex]  the first BC / uncompressed colour textures those draws bind, one dump each
+//   [dummy]  distinct shader keys that bound the host's 1x1 dummy, every 600 frames
+// The PNGs use the same directory and the same td_dump writer as the existing td_* dumps, so a
